            "review_title": "Review at Tartine Saïgon - Lumiere (An Phu) Q2",
            "review_text": "Samanths W\n5 contributions\n0\nThe food is cold!\nFeb 2026 • Couples\nWe originally looked at the menu outside the restaurant and decided to have what looked like an amazing brunch. The cafe is accessible by a lift. When we were served we were told they did not serve this menu. We both ordered the eggs Benedict and some drinks. The matcha latte, cappuccino and OJ were out of this world! The food looked amazing but the eggs were cold. The staff were brilliant and said they would get hot eggs, it wasn’t long and they returned more cold eggs! Cold poached eggs might be a thing in Vietnam but I’m sure I did ask for hot ones. The food is important. Hence the low score.\nRead more\nWritten February 18, 2026",
